Track 1: Stained Light Swallows the Rail
- Story & Context: When the lead truck of the Solder-Caravan cracked an axle across the switchyard ties at New Joliet, guitarist Silas Thornton rigged his resonator slide through a heat-fried Korg filter while blowing sand choked the glass artisans' annealing tubes. With raiders watching from the ridge and the diesel generator sputtering ozone and burning fish-glue, Silas locked into a relentless, low-end drone while Noah Vance whistled the sharp, piercing distress code of old steam engineers. The caravan beat their ammo crates against the floorboards for four continuous hours until the scouts retreated into the scrub, anchored by Silas shouting through his bullet mic, "The rails don't rust when the glass stays red!"
