Track 2: "Whose Hand Broke the Crucible?"
- Story & Context: Huddled within the canvas walls of an annealing tent near Bitter Well, synth-tinkerer Farah Al-Jamil confessed to gutting the silver wiring out of a priceless salvaged ARP Odyssey just to solder the cracked seam of a cooling glass horn. Her fingers were blistered and reeking of lamp oil as she blew a low, unearthly breath whistle over the jagged lip of a quartz container, modulating the synth’s surviving sub-bass oscillator into an agonizing, slow-motion crawl. Nobody in the caravan banished her because the hypnotic, rumbling resonance proved the only thing capable of soothing the pack animals through the midnight dust squalls, even as she wept into the overdriven tape head, "I cracked your crucible just to hear the engine cry."
