Track 3: Khadir’s Solder-Springs
- Story & Context: Decades after an electrical fire gutted the trading bazaar at Khadir’s Solder-Springs, nomads still refuse to camp near the scorched salt mounds where dozens of salvaged synthesizer chassis melted into the silica sand. Caravan chroniclers captured this field recording at dawn when gale-force sirocco winds whipped through the calcified keyboard shells, causing the corroded electronics and cracked ceramic whistle vents to whistle and hum an eternal, microtonal Chicago blues shuffle across the dunes. The track loops this phantom wind alongside a single, stubborn heel-stomp that refuses to stop marching, carrying the caravan's final recorded vow: "Sweep the ash away, but leave the iron humming."
